  "implemented": [
    "Authenticate the core Sentry from validated state.pid first, before enumerating any other PID as a possible role. Strict argv0/root flag/final job, pinned Sentry executable and actual native4096 remain mandatory.",
    "Exactly one positive Gofer argv identity is accepted with pinned runsc executable, exact job/root and native4096; duplicate Gofer candidates still fail.",
    "Raw proc observation can represent a truly empty cmdline as argv=[] plus explicit empty/byte-count/SHA fields. Malformed nonempty cmdline remains rejected.",
    "An empty argv or inherited runsc-sandbox argv is accepted only for a direct child of that authenticated core Sentry, with the same pinned Sentry executable identity, same exact cgroup, start time at least its parent, and stable PID/start/parent/argv/exe/cgroup/limits. Inherited argv must equal the full core Sentry argv exactly. No arbitrary parent chain is accepted.",
    "Native systrap children are recorded as authenticated-systrap-child, with their observed native4096 separately checked. They never replace the core Sentry or Gofer.",
    "The two actual known sidecars require pinned manifest executable and exact argv. FD-parking must be in host leaf with parent1 and no earlier than Sentry; proc-umounter must be a direct Sentry child in the same cgroup with no earlier start. Their raw native limits are retained with native_nofile_enforced_by_this_gate=false; no4096 claim is made for them.",
    "Unknown empty/nonempty helpers and Sentry-like argv mismatches reject. Every core and accepted auxiliary observation is repeated, including parent identity; pinned executable paths and final exact cgroup inventory are rechecked.",
    "The same48KiB whole serialized enforcement budget includes all auxiliary raw fields; over-budget evidence rejects before start. Profile flags, image/init, guest256 and all other resource/containment/cleanup controls are unchanged."
  ],
